1
00:00:09,634 --> 00:00:10,635
This means…

2
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,345
To spice up their marriage,

3
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,140
the wife dressed up and role-played
as different types of women.

4
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:16,433
And were going on dates?

5
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:18,184
It's a wonderful thing!

6
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:20,061
That's right, it's lovely!

7
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,312
That is what true love is.

8
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:23,022
<i>I want to get married too.</i>

9
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:26,901
<i>We're on a hard-earned vacation,</i>
<i>so we've got to find some romance.</i>

10
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:28,403
<i>Romance, huh.</i>

11
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:30,989
<i>Midori, you seriously need</i>
<i>to get a boyfriend soon!</i>

12
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:34,367
<i>Not having dated a guy at your age</i>
<i>is honestly a red flag!</i>

13
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:37,579
Let’s invite some guys over
and have a mixer at this villa!

14
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:38,830
A mixer at the villa…

15
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:40,540
Sounds just like
a reality show, I love it.

16
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,666
<i>A reality show?</i>

17
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,001
<i>Like a dating show?</i>

18
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:46,421
<i>I wonder if I'm even capable</i>
<i>of falling in love.</i>

19
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,078
Mr. Nishigami!

20
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:21,790
You picked summer oranges for us.

21
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:25,502
Leaving too many on the tree
puts a strain on it.

22
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,212
I see.

23
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:31,966
They smell so good, freshly picked!

24
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,677
I'll make freshly squeezed juice!

25
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:35,845
Right!

26
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:38,848
If you add honey,
it gets sweet and super delicious!

27
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:41,142
I bet you already knew that.

28
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:45,855
Where are Konta and the others?

29
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:49,067
My brother went grocery shopping,

30
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:52,654
and Tetsuro is fishing, I think?

31
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,490
So today is…

32
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,411
Yes! It’s a girls' day.

33
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:02,497
I see.

34
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:05,792
-Well then…
-Oh, wait…

35
00:02:09,337 --> 00:02:10,547
There he goes.

36
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:16,177
Maybe I shouldn't have said
it was a girls' day.

37
00:02:19,889 --> 00:02:22,308
It's an orange. Oh, so cute!

38
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:24,227
We really need to budget better.

39
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,395
Looks good!

40
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:30,984
Hello? Konta? What's up?

41
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:33,736
I’m buying groceries.
Do you need anything?

42
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:36,865
<i>Oh, perfect timing!</i>
<i>Just get whatever is cheap.</i>

43
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,867
<i>We'll be staying</i>
<i>at this villa for a while,</i>

44
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,202
<i>so we need to keep food expenses down.</i>

45
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,453
Got it!

46
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:47,041
Cheap stuff.

47
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:52,171
Okay, this goes on Instagram.

48
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:53,339
What?

49
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:54,382
What?

50
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:55,508
Mikako…

51
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:57,468
got married!

52
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:58,511
What?

53
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:00,305
Mikako? Our classmate?

54
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:01,180
Yes!

55
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,891
-Oh, wow.
-What?

56
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:03,975
Whoa!

57
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,685
He looks so respectable.

58
00:03:07,395 --> 00:03:10,982
Mikako totally got plastic surgery.
Doesn't her nose look smaller?

59
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:13,401
She did nothing but go to mixers in Tokyo.

60
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:15,069
Must have reeled in a good one.

61
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:18,281
Wait, hold on!

62
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:21,200
Suzuki from the class next to ours
got married too!

63
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:22,493
-Seriously?
-What?

64
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:23,912
That plain girl?

65
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:34,631
I wonder where everyone meets
their soulmates.

66
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:09,999
Cheap stuff…

67
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:13,878
Radishes? One hundred yen?

68
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:17,757
R-Radish? What?

69
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:18,883
These…

70
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,805
These are turnips. Red turnips.

71
00:04:23,888 --> 00:04:27,016
Midori told me to get whatever is cheap.
This is definitely the cheapest.

72
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:31,437
Radish, turnip, red turnip!

73
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:33,481
Oh, Midori?

74
00:04:33,564 --> 00:04:35,066
I'm heading back soon.

75
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:37,360
But listen, like, today,

76
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:40,113
these tiny little turnips
were ridiculously cheap!

77
00:04:40,196 --> 00:04:41,948
Radi? Radi…

78
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:44,450
Whatever, they're turnips!

79
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:46,494
They were practically giving them away!

80
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:48,246
So, I bought the entire stock!

81
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:51,165
I bought every single turnip!
See ya later.

82
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:52,959
What?

83
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:54,252
She hung up already.

84
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:56,170
-Man, Midori…
-Excuse me.

85
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:03,469
I wonder what Mikako's husband
makes in a year.

86
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:05,596
Maybe… like 20 million yen?

87
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,848
What?

88
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:09,183
-She doesn't have to worry about money.
-True.

89
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:13,354
I want a rich, handsome husband too.

90
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:14,480
Hey.

91
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:16,858
The new season of <i>Last Princess</i>
is streaming!

92
00:05:16,941 --> 00:05:18,568
-What?
-You love it, right, Rinrin?

93
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,111
All right, let’s watch it! Right now!

94
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:23,364
I'm in the mood for romance,
so we are watching this now!

95
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:24,574
Huh…

96
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:27,660
I haven't really watched
this kind of stuff before.

97
00:05:33,499 --> 00:05:38,546
<i>On this season of</i> Last Princess<i>,</i>
<i>our leading man is…</i>

98
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,015
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

99
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:53,019
I run multiple restaurants in Tokyo.

100
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:56,731
<i>On this journey,</i>
<i>I hope to find my ultimate partner</i>

101
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:58,566
and return to Tokyo together.

102
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:01,944
<i>Through my hobby,</i>

103
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:04,447
<i>I've built up some muscles.</i>
<i>That's my charm.</i>

104
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:09,035
<i>When your shoulders get broad like this,</i>
<i>it gives you a real sense of presence.</i>

105
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:12,997
I feel like it helps elevate me
as a business owner,

106
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:14,332
so I work hard at it.

107
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:15,249
<i>Yes.</i>

108
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,293
This guy seems super shady.

109
00:06:17,376 --> 00:06:19,045
Total meathead vibes.

110
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,631
<i>As for my type, let's see.</i>

111
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:24,675
<i>Definitely someone who laughs a lot,</i>
<i>a cheerful girl.</i>

112
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:29,055
<i>Right now, I'm extremely driven</i>
<i>when it comes to my work.</i>

113
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:32,433
<i>I'm the type to act</i>
<i>the moment I get an idea.</i>

114
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,018
<i>I don't like negative people.</i>

115
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:39,398
<i>I prefer someone cheerful</i>
<i>who can take anything positively.</i>

116
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:44,570
The woman who steals this guy's heart
gets to be the last princess!

117
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:46,656
Oh, I see.

118
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:49,325
They're looking
for someone to marry, after all!

119
00:06:49,408 --> 00:06:51,577
-Really?
-Everyone goes all out to seduce him.

120
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:54,622
-So they actually get married?
-Sometimes they do.

121
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,915
For real.

122
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:57,583
I bet it's scripted.

123
00:06:57,667 --> 00:07:00,545
Midori! If you talk like that,
you can't enjoy dating shows!

124
00:07:00,628 --> 00:07:01,838
Oh, okay.

125
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:04,715
Is she a female candidate?

126
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:24,193
<i>I'm Airi.</i>

127
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:28,072
I'm 27 years old. I work as a model.

128
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:30,450
Wow, she's gorgeous!

129
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:33,703
She's totally a pro at this romance stuff.

130
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:35,997
She's totally making it to the end.

131
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,498
She's not all that.

132
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:38,499
What?

133
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:40,918
For a reality show these days,
she's on the weaker side.

134
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:42,462
Seriously?

135
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:45,631
Nice to meet you.

136
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,091
Nice to meet you.

137
00:07:47,175 --> 00:07:48,718
-I'm Airi.
-Airi.

138
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:52,763
I came on this journey
to become your number one, Kotaro!

139
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:54,765
I'm flattered.

140
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:56,601
-Thank you.
-Cringe!

141
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:58,394
"Number one" is a cringe line?

142
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:02,440
This girl is just using this show as
a stepping stone to become a celebrity.

143
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:05,401
She has zero intention
of marrying this guy.

144
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:06,819
It’s clout chasing.

145
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:18,956
Nice to meet you.

146
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,208
Nice to meet you.

147
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:21,584
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

148
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:24,545
Hooray, hooray,

149
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:25,838
Kotaro!

150
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:29,842
A Spirit Bomb that lights up
everyone's day! I'm Moka!

151
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,761
Spirit Bomb?

152
00:08:31,844 --> 00:08:34,347
Apologize to Mr. Akira Toriyama right now!

153
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:36,307
In my daily life,

154
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:39,644
I'm a cheerleader for a basketball team
in Chiba Prefecture.

155
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:41,938
<i>He's completely my type.</i>

156
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:45,983
<i>He has such a great build</i>
<i>and he's handsome. Totally my type.</i>

157
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,236
I really want to make him mine.

158
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,531
Do you like short girls?

159
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:54,492
I do like shorter girls, yes.

160
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:57,995
Watch, Moka is going to do
the hand-size comparison thing

161
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,164
just to show off how tiny she is.

162
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:01,999
Midori, pour some alcohol! Alcohol!

163
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,834
What? You're drinking in the morning?

164
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:07,630
Turn around for a second.

165
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:09,632
-You want me to? Okay.
-Yes.

166
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:22,311
Moka only comes up to here.

167
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:25,606
You're so big.

168
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:28,651
Right, yes.

169
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,444
She exceeded my expectations.

170
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:32,280
Moka is a serious tactician.

171
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:34,407
Her power level is insane!

172
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:38,536
<i>My heart skipped a beat.</i>
<i>The physical contact was unexpected.</i>

173
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,247
She was incredibly cute.

174
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:53,467
<i>I do that a lot.</i>

175
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:56,220
It’s my best feature,

176
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:58,723
so I made sure to use it
to its full potential.

177
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:01,309
Girls like that always win.

178
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:03,978
-I used to play basketball.
-Really?

179
00:10:04,061 --> 00:10:05,855
I also really love watching pro-wrestling.

180
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:06,939
-I see.
-Yes.

181
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:09,400
-And I go to saunas a lot too.
-Saunas too?

182
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:10,651
-Yes.
-Do you like saunas?

183
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:11,819
-I love saunas.
-Wow!

184
00:10:11,902 --> 00:10:13,446
I actually really like saunas too.

185
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:15,823
-Really? We should go together.
-Yes!

186
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:18,075
-A sauna date sounds great. Yes!
-Let's do it.

187
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:21,746
I also think about saunas
from a business perspective.

188
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:25,166
I want to combine the restaurants
I run with a sauna concept.

189
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:26,917
-Wow, you're amazing!
-Not really.

190
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:28,753
Saunas are very trendy right now.

191
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:30,921
They are, they're super popular.

192
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:33,758
You're such a sharp businessman
to see opportunity in that!

193
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:37,970
There it is!
Those are staple lines of popular girls.

194
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,513
-"You're amazing!"
-"I didn't know that!"

195
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:40,890
-"Wow!"
-"You have great sense!"

196
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:42,183
"I see!"

197
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:44,810
You two are amazing!

198
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:01,410
Nice to meet you.

199
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:02,578
Nice to meet you.

200
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:04,830
-I'm Kotoko.
-Kotoko.

201
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,082
Yes.

202
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:10,252
Well, to be honest,
I quit my job to come meet you.

203
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:11,170
What?

204
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:14,965
-You quit your job?
-Yes, I did.

205
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:18,594
<i>I worked at a food manufacturer</i>
<i>for five years.</i>

206
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:22,390
Now, I've left the company,
so I am unemployed.

207
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,683
Unemployed! Just like me!

208
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:27,812
Wow, to have that level of commitment…

209
00:11:27,895 --> 00:11:28,729
Yes.

210
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,482
I'm flattered.

211
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:33,526
-Yes.
-I'm glad.

212
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:35,736
-I love bold people.
-Oh, really?

213
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,822
-Yes. I'm thrilled.
-Thank you.

214
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,825
-Actually…
-Yes?

215
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:45,371
I heard that you are
very particular about your diet.

216
00:11:45,454 --> 00:11:47,039
-Yes.
-Well…

217
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,500
What's that?

218
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:52,962
I went and got certified
as a food advisor!

219
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,630
Wait, a food advisor?

220
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:55,756
-Yes!
-Really?

221
00:11:57,299 --> 00:11:58,884
-It's the real deal.
-Incredible!

222
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:01,846
Oh, she has qualifications.

223
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,055
So she's not like me.

224
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:06,392
There are always girls like that
who collect certifications.

225
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,477
Don't worry, Midori.
You don't need any of that!

226
00:12:08,561 --> 00:12:10,187
You can make a cocktail this good!

227
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:12,857
-That's your benchmark?
-Cheers!

228
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,650
-Cheers.
-Yay.

229
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:27,288
Nice to meet you.

230
00:12:27,371 --> 00:12:28,414
Nice to meet you.

231
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:31,625
I came here to find
my very first boyfriend.

232
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:34,211
I'm Mayumi, 25 years old,
from Ibaraki Prefecture.

233
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:36,255
It's a pleasure to meet you.

234
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:39,133
Right now, I'm working part-time
while attending a training school

235
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:40,676
to become a voice actress.

236
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:44,221
Well, "first boyfriend" is a little heavy.

237
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:45,431
What?

238
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:46,599
Really?

239
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:48,726
-I look forward to getting to know you.
-Likewise.

240
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:51,687
That's wonderful. I absolutely love people
who chase their dreams.

241
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:52,938
-Really?
-Yes.

242
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:55,733
-I would like to join forces--
-Have you achieved your dreams?

243
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:58,152
-No, not even close.
-Not yet?

244
00:12:58,235 --> 00:12:59,487
I'm only halfway.

245
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:01,071
-Halfway?
-Yes!

246
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:03,532
What kind of person is your type?

247
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:08,829
Well, I like people who are like aliens.

248
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:11,165
-Aliens?
-Yes.

249
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:13,667
There it is, the quirky ditz persona.

250
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:16,962
When you can't win with a conventional
approach, you have to act weird.

251
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,882
Oh, aliens?

252
00:13:19,965 --> 00:13:20,966
That's cute.

253
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:24,762
<i>I blurted out how cute she was.</i>

254
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:28,599
She had an innocent,
carefree vibe, and I liked it.

255
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,851
Wow, she struck a chord.

256
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:34,438
Girls like her surprisingly
make it far in these shows.

257
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:42,071
I want to do my best
and get them to open their hearts.

258
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:45,366
I see. I look forward to it.

259
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:48,869
Jeez, this guy is an idiot.

260
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:50,663
Oh, speaking of which, Rinrin,

261
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:53,958
didn't you apply
for<i> Last Princess </i>a few years back?

262
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:56,752
Yes, a long time ago.

263
00:13:57,336 --> 00:14:01,006
To catch the judges' attention,
you tried to act ditzy, right?

264
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:03,717
Yes. But they just thought
I was dumb and dropped me.

265
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:05,344
What a dark past!

266
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:08,264
But if it were now,
I would totally dominate this show!

267
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:10,432
You do have plenty of dating experience.

268
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:13,060
We’re staying
in this gorgeous villa, after all.

269
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:16,188
I want to have a romance
like <i>Last Princess </i>too!

270
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:21,902
Coming!

271
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:24,280
Nice to meet you.

272
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:26,282
Who are you?

273
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:30,411
Mr. Konta invited us over!

274
00:14:31,328 --> 00:14:32,872
What?

275
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,206
Seriously?

276
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:35,624
Isn't this just like…

277
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,668
Our very own reality dating show?

278
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:39,628
-I've got to put on makeup.
-What?

279
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:41,964
-Me too!
-Huh? Wait… Well…

280
00:14:42,047 --> 00:14:43,048
Uh…

281
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:45,050
Please wait just a moment.

282
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:07,406
They smell so good, freshly picked!

283
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:41,982
<i>We came here from Tokyo.</i>

284
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,652
He said, "We're having a barbecue
at my villa, you should come."

285
00:15:44,735 --> 00:15:46,862
They're handsome and successful!

286
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:50,240
<i>-Perhaps they are…</i>
<i>-Our dating show has finally begun!</i>

287
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:53,744
<i>I'm Midori, Konta's younger sister.</i>

288
00:15:53,827 --> 00:15:57,081
<i>When it comes to cooking and cleaning,</i>
<i>I work harder than anyone!</i>

289
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,083
<i>I'm Rinrin, Midori's friend.</i>

290
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:03,420
<i>I think it's about time</i>
<i>I find that one special soulmate.</i>

291
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,089
<i>Likewise, I'm her friend, Tsumugi.</i>

292
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:08,759
<i>I came here to experience</i>
<i>the passionate love of a lifetime.</i>

293
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:10,678
<i>I don't plan on holding back.</i>

294
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:11,971
<i>-I will…</i>
<i>-Definitely…</i>

295
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:15,265
Find a good person
and go back to Tokyo with him!

296
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:16,308
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
